.TH TCGETWINSIZE 3C "Oct 02, 2026"
.SH NAME
tcgetwinsize, tcsetwinsize \- get and set the size of a terminal window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.LP
.nf
#include <termios.h>

\fBint\fR \fBtcgetwinsize\fR(\fBint\fR \fIfildes\fR, \fBconst struct winsize *\fR\fIwinsize_p\fR);
\fBint\fR \fBtcsetwinsize\fR(\fBint\fR \fIfildes\fR, \fBconst struct winsize *\fR\fIwinsize_p\fR);

.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" FIXME
.SH RETURN VALUES
.sp
.LP
.\" FIXME
Upon successful completion, \fBtcgetsid()\fR returns the process group \fBID\fR
associated with the terminal.  Otherwise, a value of \fB(pid_t)\(mi1\fR is
returned and \fBerrno\fR is set to indicate the error.
.SH ERRORS
.\" FIXME
.sp
.LP
The \fBtcgetwinsize()\fR function will fail if:
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fBEACCES\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 10n
The \fIfildes\fR argument is not associated with a controlling terminal.
.RE

.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fBEBADF\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 10n
The \fIfildes\fR argument is not a valid file descriptor.
.RE

.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fBENOTTY\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 10n
The file associated with \fIfildes\fR is not a terminal.
.RE

.SH ATTRIBUTES
.sp
.LP
See \fBattributes\fR(7) for descriptions of the following attributes:
.sp

.sp
.TS
box;
c | c
l | l .
ATTRIBUTE TYPE	ATTRIBUTE VALUE
_
Interface Stability	Standard
_
MT-Level	MT-Safe
.TE

.SH SEE ALSO
.sp
.LP
.BR termio (4I),
.BR attributes (7),
.BR standards (7)
